Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] OperationEquivalence: compare regions from an explicit stack

`OperationEquivalence::isEquivalentTo` and `isRegionEquivalentTo` call
each other once per level of region nesting, so comparing two operations
nested N deep takes N native frames of each, and a deep enough nest
overflows the stack of the thread comparing them. Both now run one
comparison that keeps its place on an explicit stack: for each pair of
operations whose regions are being compared, the pairs of regions left,
the map of the current pair's blocks, and the pair of blocks and of
operations reached. It compares in the order of the recursion, so
`checkEquivalent`, `markEquivalent` and `checkCommutativeEquivalent`
are called in the same order and the comparison stops at the same first
difference; one symbol-reference mapper serves the whole comparison.

Unit test: two chains of operations nested 10,000 deep are compared on a
256 KiB thread, their values marked equivalent in the recursion's order,
and a chain whose innermost successors differ is not equivalent.
